				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				192,
				11
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Implement atomic UI services and improve bootstrap\n\nThis commit introduces the foundational Effect-TS services for the editor workbench layout and refines the initialization sequence to ensure robust pre-load global availability.\n\nNew implementations include:\n- `ActivityBar`, `Panel`, `Sidebar`, and `StatusBar` services: These provide atomic, reactive state management for the UI shell. They utilize `SubscriptionRef` to handle item CRUD operations, active state tracking, and priority sorting via Effect-TS streams.\n- `NetworkRestrictions` service: A security-focused service that enforces network policies by default (blocking telemetry, marketplace, and update endpoints) while allowing internal `localhost` and `Mountain` communication.\n\nRefactoring and Integration:\n- Updated `Layers/Tauri.ts` to include the new UI services in the `TauriBaseLayer`, `TauriLiveLayer`, and `TauriDevLayer`, making them available to the application context.\n- Modified `Install.ts` to attach `preloadGlobals` (containing IPC, process, and config) to `window` and signal readiness via `__WIND_PRELOAD_READY__`.\n- Refactored `Sandbox.ts` initialization to switch from event-based to a polling-based strategy when awaiting pre-load globals, increasing reliability for the Effect bootstrap.\n- Minor cleanup in `IPC.ts` and reorganization of `index.ts` exports.\n\nThis change completes the transition of the editor shell's layout logic into the declarative, composable Effect-TS architecture used by `Wind`.",
			"SHA": "419ffb6fd32853b47b8524a0a25668158dbd347b"
		}
